{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_genus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_genus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Definitions","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Degree","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Monic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chebyshev_degree_genus","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/chebyshev_degree_genus.lean#L131-L147","doc":"**Chebyshev degree equals Seifert genus** ([`lem:chebyshev-degree-genus`]).\n\nFor every odd positive `p`, the Hecke recurrence polynomial `a p`\nhas `natDegree (a p) = p − 1` (twice the Seifert genus\n`g(T_{2,p}) = (p − 1)/2`) and leading coefficient `1`.\n\n**Derived** from `hecke_deg_monic` (degree + monicity); the `odd`\nhypothesis fixes the torus-knot family `T_{2,p}` for the genus\ninterpretation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:chebyshev-degree-genus","label":"lem:chebyshev-degree-genus","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/chebyshev-degree-genus.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hecke_deg_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hecke_deg_monic","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/chebyshev_degree_genus.lean#L92-L129","doc":"**Degree / monicity of the Hecke recurrence** (the substantive\ncontent).  For every `n ≥ 1`, `a n` is monic with\n`natDegree (a n) = n − 1`.  Proved by strong induction:\n`X · a (n+1)` is monic of degree `n+1`, and `a n` has strictly\nsmaller degree, so their sum is monic of degree `n+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hecke_deg_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hecke_deg_le","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/chebyshev_degree_genus.lean#L63-L90","doc":"Degree upper bound: `natDegree (a n) ≤ n − 1` for every `n`.\n\nUsed in the inductive step of `hecke_deg_monic` to show that the\n`a n` term is strictly dominated by `X · a (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeRecurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeRecurrence","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/chebyshev_degree_genus.lean#L52-L61","doc":"The Hecke recurrence `a` over `Polynomial ℤ`, indexed by ℕ.\n\n`a 0 = 0`, `a 1 = 1`, `a (n+2) = X · a (n+1) + a n`.\nThese are the Chebyshev-like polynomials whose specialisation at\n`s = q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}` recovers the Markov-trace evaluations of\nthe torus-knot family `T_{2,n}` in the Iwahori–Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0}]}